{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books","id":998087,"title":"The \"Must Have\" books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T22:02:39-07:00","id":998087,"title":"The \"Must Have\" books","content":"Im not speaking of the basic Core-Storyteller-Player's guide for books. im speaking more of those who can change drastically your game/setting view/setting etc... Which ones would you recommend? even if they are not of the game you are currently running?.<br /> <br /> Personally, for all my WoD games i try to keep in mind &quot;Destiny's Price&quot; for urban settings.<br /> Also, whenever i dont use the Werewolf Mythos, i tend to re read Days of Fire (im a firm believer that if Demons are Involved, things got Fucked up).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T01:48:38-07:00","id":998142,"title":"","content":"Book of the Wyrm. I haven't read them all, I think there's nearly one for each edition, but 20th is pretty solid (bar the weird inclusion of feminists and women's medicine in an otherwise evil linup of Magadon subsidiaries, and an electric car that saves the planet)<br /> <br /> Hunters the hunted. (II) Tons of information on humans sorting your shit out on their own. Humans are always a viable enemy, even though this is a vampire-biased book.<br /> <br /> I feel like the two of these really help with the backdrop of the world of darkness. Both are a must for all gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-04-2016, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:16:33-07:00","id":998809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998142#post998142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(bar the weird inclusion of feminists and women's medicine in an otherwise evil linup of Magadon subsidiaries</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that, too. I'm learning to ignore things like that in Onyx Path books. <br /> <br /> And Hunters Hunted 2 is really, REALLY great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:26:27-07:00","id":998907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998142#post998142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of the Wyrm. I haven't read them all, I think there's nearly one for each edition, but 20th is pretty solid (bar the weird inclusion of feminists and<br /> women's medicine in an otherwise evil linup of Magadon subsidiaries, and an electric car that saves the planet)</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that could possibly be wrong with that section is that no one in that section knowingly serves the Wyrm. I think the word &quot;knowingly&quot; is pretty important in that sentence, however. They probably do serve the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=women%27s+medicine&amp;ie=utf-8&amp;oe=utf-8\" target=\"_blank\">Real world women's medicine is a real thing.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:46:12-07:00","id":998919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998907#post998907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=women%27s+medicine&amp;ie=utf-8&amp;oe=utf-8\" target=\"_blank\">Real world women's medicine is a real thing.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is questioning that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:48:32-07:00","id":998921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998919#post998919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone is questioning that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not, although I would argue otherwise. When the response to seeing an actual description of the actual forms women's medicine takes, is &quot;Why is there feminism in my RPG?&quot; then it looks to me like someone is <i>indeed</i> questioning that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:01:16-07:00","id":998928,"title":"","content":"The Demon Player's Guide. It's pretty much &quot;Demon: The Fallen: The rest of it&quot;. Merits and flaws, rituals, DIY Apocalypse Forms, expanded Relics and some background stuff to flesh out the lore of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:03:39-07:00","id":998993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998921#post998921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not, although I would argue otherwise. When the response to seeing an actual description of the actual forms women's medicine takes, is &quot;Why is there feminism in my RPG?&quot; then it looks to me like someone is <i>indeed</i> questioning that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Women's medicine and femenists isn't the issue. The issue was the context. <br /> <br /> EVIL<br /> EVIL<br /> EVIL<br /> INSIDIOUSLY EVIL<br /> Women's medicine<br /> EVIL<br /> MORE EVIL<br /> <br /> (also, the writting style/quality changed for that little addition, so I'm guessing someone just wanted to voice someone's opinion in someone else's piece, ignorant of the context)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:35:30-07:00","id":999003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998993#post998993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Women's medicine and femenists isn't the issue. The issue was the context.<br /> <br /> EVIL<br /> EVIL<br /> EVIL<br /> INSIDIOUSLY EVIL<br /> Women's medicine<br /> EVIL<br /> MORE EVIL<br /> <br /> (also, the writting style/quality changed for that little addition, so I'm guessing someone just wanted to voice someone's opinion in someone else's piece, ignorant of the context)</div> </div> </div> </div>Magadon's writeup in the W20 Book of the Wyrm is a condensed version of its writeup in Subsidiaries. Said NPC is from Subsidiaries, so complaining about it now is being a bit like a certain pink-colored Pokemon. The elements that did get in might be a bit lopsided, a lot of things about its entry in Subsidiaries were lopsided, like antidepressants being able to curb and permanently stifle Rage, or the extreme lethality of chemical weapons, even to Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T00:10:45-07:00","id":999098,"title":"","content":"The following aren't necessarily all books that you'll want to run from or even great but they provide bold, broad samples of different flavours you can adapt:<br /> <br /> The Giovanni Chronicles 1 &amp; 2 (Formative events of the modern V:TM world)<br /> Gehenna: The Final Nights (An interesting look in to the ways you can play with canon)<br /> Ghoul: Fatal Addiction (A disturbing insight in to the condition)<br /> Constantinople By Night (An exploration of good intentions, failure and corruption)<br /> Transylvania Chronicles 4 (An interesting look at the power games of ancients and the risk factor the nuclear age presents to and with vampires)<br /> Clanbook Baali (A look at monster's monsters)<br /> Montreal By Night (An interesting exercise in excess)<br /> Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand (A bad book but an important look at just how badly wrong attempts to rewrite the universe can go)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 11-06-2016, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:49:06-08:00","id":999237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998087-the-must-have-books?p=998921#post998921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not, although I would argue otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, but as Flower, Innocent stated, that is simply not what he was saying. I didn't take it that way, either. You did. That's okay. <br /> <br /> It doesn't take away from what is pretty much a FANTASTIC book by Onyx Path and their Werewolf writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 11-06-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}